WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.210
CPAC is the Conservative Political Action
Conference.

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:09.871
It culminated yesterday in an erratic and
delusional crescendo with former President

00:00:09.871 --> 00:00:13.450
Donald Trump's first speech since leaving
office on January 20th.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:19.470
The speech started, of course, 70 minutes
late for no good reason, endlessly delayed,

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.820
and was rife with all of the things we would
expect from Donald Trump.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.890
Lies about what he did, lies about what he
didn't do, lies about what Joe Biden has done

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:33.740
so far, lies about what Joe Biden has not
done so far, lies about immigrants, lies about

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:41.520
covid, lies about the economy of victimhood,
complex that would be worthy of a few decades

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:42.520
of psychoanalysis.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:48.270
And, of course, yes, false claims that Donald
Trump actually won the election.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:52.910
The speech was expected to be a Fidel Castro
like two hours or more.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:54.660
In the end, it was about 90 minutes.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:00.050
Trump appeared to sort of skip a bunch of
the end when he and the crowd seemed increasingly

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.399
bored by the things that he was saying.

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:05.390
The crowd was also bored and silent during
many parts of the speech.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:06.560
They were most riled up.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.770
And this tells you a lot about the state of
the Republican Party.

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:14.390
The crowd most titillated when Trump called
covid the China virus.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.630
They erupted with a standing ovation when
Trump claimed he won the election, the crowd

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.630
went nuts.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:24.430
And when Trump talked about the new wedge
issue of transgender women in sports, the

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.430
crowd also gave a standing ovation.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:29.620
Those were the things that were most interesting
to the crowd.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:32.320
I can't possibly cover the whole speech.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.570
I want to touch on some key moments.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:39.410
Donald Trump opened the speech by claiming
that his presidency was the most successful

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:40.619
in history.

00:01:40.619 --> 00:01:45.030
Despite losing and becoming one of only 10
one term presidents.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:50.000
Trump says his was the most successful to
so many wonderful friends, conservatives and

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.270
fellow citizens in this room and all across
our country.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:02:01.030
I stand before you today to declare that the
incredible journey we began together, we went

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:02.970
through a journey like nobody else.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.900
There's never been a journey like it.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.970
There's never been a journey so successful.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:11.270
We began it together four years ago.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:18.360
Interesting to take a presidency with no accomplishments,
a globally humiliating failure on the pandemic

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.390
and a huge electoral loss.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.980
And call it the most successful.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.560
But OK, the crowd, I guess, liked it.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:29.110
Most importantly, Donald Trump making it clear
he is not starting a new party.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:34.280
And the president, the former president rightly
identifies that starting a new party would

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.520
make Republicans lose for a long time.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.970
We're not starting new parties.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:45.520
You know, they kept saying he's going to start
a brand new party.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:50.450
We have the Republican Party, it's going to
unite and be stronger than ever before.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:53.819
I am not starting a new party.

00:02:53.819 --> 00:02:55.090
That was fake news.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.580
Fake news now.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:59.190
Wouldn't that be brilliant?

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:03.569
Let's start a new party and let's divide our
vote so that you can never win.

00:03:03.569 --> 00:03:05.129
No, we're not interested in that.

00:03:05.129 --> 00:03:08.260
So Trump's analysis there is correct.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:12.730
The best assessment is the reports were accurate
at the time.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:17.480
Trump was thinking of starting a new party,
but he was talked out a bit for this reason

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:21.380
that it would fracture the right and they
wouldn't win for a very long time, which was

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:24.250
also our assessment of that idea.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:30.140
As usual, Donald Trump cites out of context
and apparently meaningless polling numbers

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.660
about how popular he is.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.150
He can't get away from this.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.650
Take a listen.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:38.590
Mr. McGlocklin just gave me numbers that nobody's
ever heard of before.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:39.750
More popular than anybody.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:40.930
That's all of us.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:42.110
It's all of us.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.110
Those are great numbers.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:44.640
And I want to thank you very much.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:45.720
Those are incredible numbers.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:51.750
I came here and he was giving me 95 percent,
97 percent, 92 percent.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:57.040
No one has ever been more popular than Trump,
according to Mr. McLachlin.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:02.370
The reality is Trump is the only president
never to poll 50 percent approval throughout

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:09.120
his presidency and the only president to leave
office with an approval so low it was 29 percent

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:12.110
approval when Donald Trump left office.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:19.039
And then after all of these lies, Donald Trump
pulls out the big lie that he won and maybe

00:04:19.039 --> 00:04:23.960
he will even win the presidential election
a third time, alluding to maybe running in

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.470
2024.

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:29.400
And the crowd goes nuts, but who knows?

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.039
Who knows?

00:04:31.039 --> 00:04:37.319
I may even decide to beat them for a third
time.

00:04:37.319 --> 00:04:39.349
OK.

00:04:39.349 --> 00:04:47.650
Importantly, though, Donald Trump did not
announce his 2024 candidacy, it was rumored

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:53.210
he might at yesterday's speech, he said he
might run and that we'll see.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.770
We'll get to that later.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:58.819
Trump again claims that if the election had
been fair, he would have won.

00:04:58.819 --> 00:05:04.050
I said it had we had a fair election.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.210
The results would have been much different.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:13.379
And then Donald Trump launched another brutal
but completely ignorant attack on wind power.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:14.550
You knew he would do it.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:15.909
How bad is wind power?

00:05:15.909 --> 00:05:17.599
So I talk about it all the time.

00:05:17.599 --> 00:05:19.580
Like we went to CPAC.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.150
Remember last as I said, we're going to watch
the president.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:26.740
Well, unless the wind is blowing, I don't
believe we'll have any electricity.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:28.439
Remember, we would we would kick.

00:05:28.439 --> 00:05:30.539
But I wasn't actually kidding.

00:05:30.539 --> 00:05:35.000
It's such an and it's such an expensive form
of energy.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.190
It's so bad for the environment.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.740
It kills the birds.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.809
It destroys the landscapes.

00:05:40.809 --> 00:05:45.710
And remember, these are structural columns
with fans on them.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:46.819
They wear out.

00:05:46.819 --> 00:05:49.590
And when they wear out all over the country,
you see them.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:50.629
Nobody takes them down.

00:05:50.629 --> 00:05:51.629
They're rotting.

00:05:51.629 --> 00:05:52.629
They're rusting.

00:05:52.629 --> 00:05:55.490
How this is environmentally good for our country.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:06:00.179
And it costs many, many times more than natural
gas, which is clean.

00:06:00.179 --> 00:06:03.240
It costs many more to and can fuel our great
factories.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:04.270
Wind can't do that.

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:08.619
And clearly, Donald Trump understanding nothing
about wind power.

00:06:08.619 --> 00:06:09.930
That's the take away.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.319
A wind power is bad for the environment.

00:06:12.319 --> 00:06:16.960
And he says it kills birds, that it's not
bad for the environment.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:24.069
Wind turbines do kill some birds, but fossil
fuel power kills way more animals.

00:06:24.069 --> 00:06:27.089
And Trump doesn't seem to care about that
at all.

00:06:27.089 --> 00:06:31.099
It's merely a talking point that does well
with the uninformed crowd.

00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:36.300
Then Donald Trump again claims he won the
election twice and the crowd just loves it

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:39.340
and famous for the rest of their lives.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:40.889
We won the election twice.

00:06:40.889 --> 00:06:47.289
I mean, you know, think about the task for
our movement.

00:06:47.289 --> 00:06:54.550
And then Donald Trump introducing the new
wedge issue gets a standing ovation.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:57.809
The issue is trans women in sports.

00:06:57.809 --> 00:06:59.180
No, I think it's crazy.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.389
I think it's just crazy what's happening.

00:07:01.389 --> 00:07:03.830
We must protect the integrity of women's sports.

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:13.729
So important after.

00:07:13.729 --> 00:07:20.419
He then went into a mildly trans phobic rant
about that issue and the crowd reenergized

00:07:20.419 --> 00:07:21.419
by that.

00:07:21.419 --> 00:07:23.430
Now, this next part is really important.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:25.110
Donald Trump is not starting his own party.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:31.569
I mentioned that earlier, but he's going out
hard against Republicans.

00:07:31.569 --> 00:07:33.779
He doesn't like Republicans.

00:07:33.779 --> 00:07:36.639
He sees as not loyal enough to him.

00:07:36.639 --> 00:07:41.099
And he calls out a long list of Republican
senators and members of the House here.

00:07:41.099 --> 00:07:47.520
Democrats don't have grandstanders like Mitt
Romney, little Ben Sasse, Richard Burr, Bill

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:57.029
Cassidy, Susan Collins, Lisa Murkowski, Pat
Toomey.

00:07:57.029 --> 00:08:08.759
And in the House, Tom Rice, South Carolina,
Adam Kinzinger, Dan Newhouse, Anthony Gonzalez,

00:08:08.759 --> 00:08:10.659
that's another beauty.

00:08:10.659 --> 00:08:19.860
Fred Upton, Jami Herrera Butler, Peter Meyer,
John Katka, David Valadao and of course, the

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:25.889
war monger, a person that loves seeing our
troops fighting Liz Cheney.

00:08:25.889 --> 00:08:29.119
How about that?

00:08:29.119 --> 00:08:34.279
So while Donald Trump did recognize that starting
his own party would be bad for the right,

00:08:34.279 --> 00:08:38.860
he apparently doesn't think that attacking
other Republicans will be bad for the right.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:39.860
Maybe he's right.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:40.860
I don't know.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:42.289
I guess we'll have to wait and see what impact
that has.

00:08:42.289 --> 00:08:50.620
But Trump going very hard against other Republicans
and then Trump plugging a website where you

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:52.389
can give money.

00:08:52.389 --> 00:08:57.790
He now says he's committed to helping Republicans
in 2022.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:00.920
And he has a Web site where you can donate
more money.

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:02.389
He pitches that next.

00:09:02.389 --> 00:09:07.690
There's only one way to contribute to our
efforts to elect America.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:11.529
First, Republican conservatives and in turn,
to make America great again.

00:09:11.529 --> 00:09:16.000
And that's through Save America PAC and Donald
J. Trump Dotcom.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:20.259
So go out there and do whatever you can because
we're going to help a lot of great people

00:09:20.259 --> 00:09:28.290
now based on his grifting tens of millions
of dollars to, quote, fight the election results,

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:32.050
which he just kept for himself just months
ago.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:36.600
I'm skeptical that your donations to this
new grift are really going to go to what he

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:38.500
claims they're going to go for.

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:43.519
And then as the speech started winding down
nearly 90 minutes after it started, Donald

00:09:43.519 --> 00:09:47.310
Trump teasing that he might run in 2024.

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:50.199
With your help, we will take back the house.

00:09:50.199 --> 00:09:58.610
We will win the Senate, and then a Republican
president will make a triumphant return to

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:01.510
the White House.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:14.541
And I wonder who that will be.

00:10:14.541 --> 00:10:17.639
Who who will that be, I wonder?

00:10:17.639 --> 00:10:27.310
So, yeah, the important takeaways Trump has
learned nothing, he's still repeating the

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:30.910
same lies, the crowd still mostly loves it.

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:33.110
So maybe it's the correct lies to repeat.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:34.589
I don't know.

00:10:34.589 --> 00:10:41.149
He's not yet committed to running in 2024,
but he's not starting his own party.

00:10:41.149 --> 00:10:48.300
And he's very willing to attack Republicans
who don't 100 percent lay down for Trump to

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:49.399
walk all over them.

00:10:49.399 --> 00:10:51.639
Those are the takeaways.

00:10:51.639 --> 00:10:59.120
And beyond that, the bit players during the
entire CPAC weekend mostly sucked up to Donald

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:02.740
Trump or at least avoided direct criticism
of Donald Trump.

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:08.350
So the overall takeaway is this remains the
party of Trump for the time being.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:13.010
And Mitt Romney's statement last week that
the nomination is Trump's, if he wants it,

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:17.769
in 2024, as of today, March 1st still holds
true.

00:11:17.769 --> 00:11:18.769
Things can change.

00:11:18.769 --> 00:11:25.720
I still think that if a lot of these Trump
being elected officials like a Bobert, Marjorie

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:31.379
Taylor Green, Madison Cawthorn, now accused
by like 30 women of harassment during college.

00:11:31.379 --> 00:11:37.439
If they go down in flames in 2022, it starts
to change the picture for Trump in 2024.

00:11:37.439 --> 00:11:39.510
But we're getting ahead of ourselves.

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:42.590
After the break, we'll look at a few other
key moments from CPAC.

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:43.980
There weren't that many.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:47.790
And we'll also have more coverage of the coverage
of this on the show's Instagram page.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:52.189
